+Codex's Git clone of a marketplace can time out on a slow connection, so the
+installer runs a failed Codex `marketplace add` or `marketplace upgrade` once
+more after five seconds, with a `retrying` row, and stops with Codex's exit
+status only when the second try fails too. An installed plugin is updated
+rather than installed again, because a host asked to install a plugin it
+already has leaves it as it is; the update is what moves it. Claude Code
+applies the update on its next start. A plugin moves only when its manifest
+version does, because a host caches a plugin by that version.
 
 `pipx` installs a copy of the source rather than a link to your checkout, so
